%u.%u.%u.%u␀␀␀␀It will see your chats and contacts, and can send messages, change settings and control this screen.␀␀␀␀Allow once␀␀Always allow␀␀␀␀No networks found (2.4 GHz only)␀␀␀␀Conversations␀␀␀î…”␀No conversations yet␀␀␀␀Pick a contact or a private channel, then give it a pad: generate one and export it to the SD card for the other device, or import theirs.␀␀New conversation␀␀␀␀no pad␀␀Tap to add a pad␀␀␀␀%lu.%lu kHz SF%u␀␀␀␀%lu.%lu kHz␀ï”™  ␀␀␀ï€‡  ␀␀␀ï¹  ␀␀␀*  Unfav␀␀␀␀*  Favorite␀ï€Œ  Unblock␀␀␀␀listens and sends␀␀␀listens␀MediaMesh%s%s, %s␀␀␀ï¹  Join␀␀␀ïƒ   Open chat␀␀ï€“  Admin␀␀ï€¡  Ping␀␀␀ïƒ   Message␀␀␀␀ï‰  Telemetry␀␀ï„¤  Show on map␀␀␀␀ï„¤  Hound␀␀ï„¤  Trace SNR␀␀ï‡«  Range test␀ï„¤  Sightline␀␀ïŒ„  Nickname␀␀␀ï„¤  Stop sharing loc␀␀␀ï„¤  Share my loc␀␀␀ï¹  Reset path␀ï‚“  Share contact␀␀Unfavorite it first␀Not in your contacts␀␀␀␀Self  %.4f, %.4f␀␀␀␀Backlight␀␀␀Medium␀␀F11 on the keyboard steps through these too.␀␀␀␀Keyboard backlight␀␀Keyboard layouts␀␀␀␀Tap the language key (EN) on the on-screen keyboard to cycle through the layouts you turn on.␀␀␀Typing␀␀Pick accented letters as you type. Off is plain typing.␀Accent popups␀␀␀Up to three words over the message that finish or fix the one you're typing, or come next; tap one to use it. Your own words and phrases come first.␀␀␀␀Predictive text␀With Predictive text on, Space fixes or finishes a word that isn't one, as on a phone. Backspace straight after puts back what you typed.␀␀␀Space completes the word␀␀␀␀Dictionary: %d words.␀␀␀Dictionary: downloads over Wi-Fi the first time, or copy dictionaries/words-en.pwd to the SD card's predict folder. Until then, your own words are suggested.␀␀␀Custom (manual)␀Client repeat is on, so radio2 runs MediaMesh beside the off-grid channel (800 kHz above it, 250 kHz SF7) and photos and voice go there. radio2 goes back to how it was when Client repeat is turned off.␀␀␀Client repeat is on, so radio2 is Off: everything, photos and voice too, goes out on the off-grid main radio. radio2 goes back to how it was when Client repeat is turned off.␀␀Picking one applies it straight away.␀␀␀Community preset␀␀␀␀TX dBm␀␀AF␀␀SF is the spreading factor, CR the coding rate, AF the airtime factor. A field applies when you leave it.␀␀␀Max duty cycle␀␀Time on air␀radio2 (MediaMesh)␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. Its SX1262 signals a packet through an I/O expander, not straight to the processor, so it can't hop between two frequencies quickly enough. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. It needs an SX1262, LR1110, LR1121 or LR2021 radio. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀A second frequency the radio switches to and from, listening and sending there.␀Photos & voice␀␀Photos & voice: Open TAK photos and voice clips, text stays on the main mesh. Per contact or channel: their Radio setting.␀␀Sent on radio2␀␀MediaMesh's preset: 250 kHz, SF7, CR 4/5. Everyone on radio2 must use the same.␀Preset␀␀Relay what this radio hears on radio2, on radio2, like a MediaMesh repeater. Main-mesh traffic isn't relayed (that's Client repeat). Needs radio2 On.␀␀␀Repeat MediaMesh␀␀␀␀Find MediaMesh␀␀Listening...␀␀␀␀Find MediaMesh asks nearby repeaters for their radio2 settings. When none say, it listens on the 250 kHz preset for about 10 s while they're asked to answer: MediaMesh repeaters answer on radio2 too.␀Everyone sharing radio2 must use the same settings. The radio switches between both frequencies, so heavy radio2 traffic costs some main-mesh reception.␀␀␀␀Listen main / radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 preamble␀Switch time␀Packets main / radio2␀␀␀Warnings␀␀␀␀Temporary radio2␀␀␀␀Use other radio2 settings for a while, for example to meet another group. They end on their own or on a restart; the settings above come back.␀␀15 min␀␀2 hours␀Use these for␀␀␀Running now␀Fast MediaMesh␀␀Repair packets that mend every listener's gaps at once, and closer packet spacing through repeaters. Switch off to go back to the way transfers worked before.␀␀Packets learn to go closer together while the farthest listeners lose almost none, and back off as soon as they lose more. Needs Fast MediaMesh. Switch off for the spacing as it was.␀␀Adaptive spacing␀␀␀␀Photos, voice messages and push-to-talk on Public and #public. Everyone on the mesh shares these channels, so this is off by default.␀␀␀Photos and voice on Public␀␀Only switch this on in an emergency.␀␀␀␀Battery and sensor readings, for nodes that ask. Your location has its own setting below.␀␀␀Answer telemetry requests␀␀␀Most mesh spam is a single character, because it is the cheapest message to send. Dropped silently: no chat entry, no notification, no sound.␀␀␀Ignore 1-character messages␀Apps like MeshCore Open TAK send photos, voice and team tracking as text. Messages between apps are dropped, and the rest become a short label such as Photo. A connected phone app still gets everything.␀␀Hide MediaMesh and TAK texts␀␀␀␀Location sharing␀␀␀␀Chosen contacts only␀␀␀␀Anyone who asks␀Sent only when that contact asks, encrypted to them. Nothing is broadcast. Needs "Answer telemetry requests" on. Pick contacts in a contact's menu.␀Share my location when asked␀␀␀␀Off sends them the shifted position your adverts use (GPS > Location privacy).␀␀Exact position to those contacts␀␀␀␀Routing␀1 byte␀␀2 bytes␀3 bytes␀More bytes tell repeaters apart in a big mesh. Repeaters older than MeshCore 1.14 drop 2 and 3 byte packets.␀␀␀␀Multi-byte routing (path hash)␀␀#region␀Region scope (#tag, blank = none)␀␀␀Channel-specific regions can be set in each channel's settings.␀Turn on only if your repeater re-floods just one region. Otherwise it can block logins and direct messages across regions.␀␀Scope direct msgs to region␀Internal (on-board)
External (MMCX)
Auto (legacy, per transmit)␀Only pick External with an antenna fitted to the external socket. After a reboot it starts on the on-board antenna, unless the switch below is on.␀␀LoRa antenna (P4)␀␀␀Starts on the external socket at every boot. Only for an antenna that stays connected.␀␀Always use the external antenna (MMCX)␀␀Reads packets on a background task so a busy screen can't drop them.␀␀␀␀Buffered receive (experimental)␀Resends a message until a repeater echoes it or the recipient ACKs. Turn off to send once only.␀Retry sends until heard␀Signal probe␀␀␀␀Sends a zero-hop advert when no neighbour has been heard for a while, so the signal reading stays fresh. Neighbours only; nothing is repeated.␀␀Minutes, 1 to 1440.␀Auto advert␀Open Advertise app␀␀Send an advert now, or set how often you re-advertise.␀␀Off silences everything below.␀␀A higher-pitched chime, louder on most buzzers.␀Loud alerts␀ï¨␀Volume␀␀Vibration␀␀␀Buzz for new messages, even with Sound off. Respects Do Not Disturb.␀␀␀␀Vibrate␀Pulse␀␀␀Gentle␀␀Long␀␀␀␀Plays once for a message, twice for a DM, three times for an @ mention. Tap one to feel it.␀Pattern␀Voice messages␀␀1200 (default)␀␀1600␀␀␀␀3200␀␀␀␀Codec2 bit rate. Higher is clearer but takes longer to send: 1600 uses a third more airtime than 1200, 3200 nearly three times as much. Every VE3 app plays all three.␀␀Recording quality␀␀␀Fills in the treble Codec2 leaves out, so voices sound less muffled. Made on the radio from the voice itself; turn off to hear clips as decoded.␀␀␀␀Brighter voice␀␀AI voice restorer␀␀␀Download voice model␀␀␀␀Play a sound for␀␀␀␀Messages␀␀␀␀Direct messages␀A mention has its own sound and switch, so it can get through when messages are quiet.␀␀@ mentions␀␀Silences the message sounds between these times every day. Messages still arrive.␀␀␀+30m␀␀␀␀-30m␀␀␀␀From␀␀␀␀Until␀␀␀MediaMesh: %s␀␀␀MAIN␀␀␀␀RADIO2␀␀Live␀␀␀␀Heard main / radio2␀Sent main / radio2␀␀Share of packets heard on radio2␀␀␀␀Preamble main / radio2␀␀Profile switches␀␀␀␀radio2 profile␀␀On listens and sends on radio2. Applies with the button below.␀␀Preamble␀␀␀␀Leave the preamble empty and the repeater picks it. Everyone on radio2 must use the same settings.␀␀Apply to repeater␀␀␀î“²␀Replies to admins␀␀␀Both␀␀␀␀Main␀␀␀␀Auto␀␀␀␀Where logins, CLI answers and ACKs go out. Both is the default.␀For Both or radio2 while radio2 is set to Listen.␀␀␀Also on a listen-only radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 can't send right now, so replies only go out on the main radio.␀␀Runs the profile above without saving it, for example to meet another group. The saved radio2 comes back after, or on a reboot.␀1 h␀2 h␀6 h␀Asking the repeater...␀␀Send advert now␀Chat history␀␀␀␀250␀500␀1000␀␀␀␀2000␀␀␀␀No limit␀␀␀␀Older messages in a chat are dropped past this. A very large or unlimited history makes the chat list slower.␀␀␀Keep per chat␀␀␀After this many failed background saves the chat is saved straight away, which can stutter the screen for a moment. Off keeps retrying in the background.␀␀␀Save in the foreground after␀␀␀␀Linked images␀␀␀A link to a picture (.jpg, .png, .gif, .webp) in a channel or a DM is downloaded while Wi-Fi is on and shown in its bubble; tap it to see it full size. The picture's server sees this radio's address. Kept on the SD card when there is one.␀␀Download over Wi-Fi␀A GIF plays, small, in its bubble. Off: its still shows; tap it to play.␀␀␀␀Play GIFs in chat␀␀␀Text console␀␀␀␀Experimental. Boots into a text console with no graphical interface: type commands, read replies. Type 'ui' there to come back; if it ever fails to start, the device returns here on its own. Turning it on or off restarts.␀␀␀%s 00m00s
